WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.375 --> 00:00:13.882
Kaitlyn was practicing her pitching at the baseball field.

2
00:00:13.883 --> 00:00:17.114
She reached into her bucket for another ball.

3
00:00:17.115 --> 00:00:21.365
Suddenly—beep, beep, beep!

4
00:00:21.366 --> 00:00:24.912
A big truck backed slowly onto the field.

5
00:00:24.913 --> 00:00:29.258
"Hey!" Kaitlyn thought. "What's that doing here?"

6
00:00:29.259 --> 00:00:34.999
A man got out of the truck. "Sorry," he said.

7
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:38.890
"We need to set up here for tonight's fireworks display.

8
00:00:38.891 --> 00:00:41.786
You'll have to move somewhere else."

9
00:00:41.787 --> 00:00:46.692
"The Fourth of July show is still hours away," Kaitlyn said.

10
00:00:46.693 --> 00:00:49.860
"Can't I practice my pitching some more?"

11
00:00:49.861 --> 00:00:52.970
"I'm afraid not," the man said.

12
00:00:52.971 --> 00:00:56.999
"It takes several hours to set up a fireworks display."

13
00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:59.995
By now more men had arrived.

14
00:00:59.996 --> 00:01:03.664
They were moving wooden racks and boxes onto the field.

15
00:01:03.665 --> 00:01:09.249
Kaitlyn sighed. She looked closely at a rack.

16
00:01:09.250 --> 00:01:14.579
It held short plastic pipes. "Those are fireworks?"

17
00:01:14.580 --> 00:01:16.700
"Nope," the man said.

18
00:01:16.701 --> 00:01:20.815
"Those are cannons that shoot the fireworks into the sky."

19
00:01:20.816 --> 00:01:25.200
He opened a box and took out a brown object wrapped in plastic.

20
00:01:25.201 --> 00:01:29.454
It was about the size of a baseball and looked like a little bomb.

21
00:01:29.455 --> 00:01:32.352
"This is a firework shell."

22
00:01:32.353 --> 00:01:35.599
"What's inside of it?" Kaitlyn asked.

23
00:01:35.600 --> 00:01:38.192
"I'll explain," said the man.

24
00:01:38.193 --> 00:01:41.559
He set the shell gently back into the box.

25
00:01:41.560 --> 00:01:45.937
Then he bent down and drew a big circle in the dirt.

26
00:01:45.938 --> 00:01:51.241
"A shell is filled with little balls of gunpowder.

27
00:01:51.242 --> 00:01:56.048
Pyrotechnicians, like me, call these balls 'stars.'"

28
00:01:56.049 --> 00:02:01.262
He picked up some baseballs and formed a pattern inside the circle with them.

29
00:02:01.263 --> 00:02:05.546
"The pattern of the stars gives a firework its shape."

30
00:02:05.547 --> 00:02:09.670
"What gives a firework its color?" Kaitlyn asked.

31
00:02:09.671 --> 00:02:14.017
"Magic!" The man laughed.

32
00:02:14.018 --> 00:02:18.372
Kaitlyn didn't. She really wanted to know the answer!

33
00:02:18.373 --> 00:02:22.790
"Well, the magic of science," the man added quickly.

34
00:02:22.791 --> 00:02:27.924
"Pyrotechnicians add chemicals to the gunpowder stars.

35
00:02:27.925 --> 00:02:31.715
When these chemicals burn, they make different colors.

36
00:02:31.716 --> 00:02:38.009
Like chemicals containing copper, for example—can you guess what color they make when they burn?"

37
00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:43.967
Kaitlyn pulled a penny from her pocket and glanced at it. "Orangish brown?"

38
00:02:43.968 --> 00:02:45.930
"Nope!" the man said.

39
00:02:45.931 --> 00:02:48.617
"Chemicals with copper make blue.

40
00:02:48.618 --> 00:02:51.357
Chemicals with calcium make orange."

41
00:02:51.358 --> 00:02:55.340
Next the man drew a square attached to the circle.

42
00:02:55.341 --> 00:02:59.627
"There's even more gunpowder here at the bottom of the shell."

43
00:02:59.628 --> 00:03:03.024
He drew a long line from the center of the circle.

44
00:03:03.025 --> 00:03:07.502
"This is the fuse. It's a string that lights the shell.

45
00:03:07.503 --> 00:03:13.389
When the shell is in the cannon, the fuse lights the gunpowder at the bottom of the shell.

46
00:03:13.390 --> 00:03:18.255
That explosion pushes the shell out of the cannon and into the air."

47
00:03:18.256 --> 00:03:21.310
"The shell doesn't burst inside the cannon?"

48
00:03:21.311 --> 00:03:25.353
"Nope. The fuse continues to burn in the air.

49
00:03:25.354 --> 00:03:29.715
Finally it explodes the shell and lights the stars.

50
00:03:29.716 --> 00:03:33.402
That's when you see the firework in the sky."

51
00:03:33.403 --> 00:03:36.251
"Awesome," Kaitlyn said.

52
00:03:36.252 --> 00:03:40.828
"Hmm. I guess you do have a lot to do before tonight."

53
00:03:40.829 --> 00:03:44.866
"Right. It's a big show with many fireworks!

54
00:03:44.867 --> 00:03:48.096
And we have to work carefully and safely.

55
00:03:48.097 --> 00:03:51.544
Working with fireworks is very dangerous."

56
00:03:51.545 --> 00:03:54.615
The man helped Kaitlyn gather her baseballs.

57
00:03:54.616 --> 00:04:00.670
"Are you going to watch the display tonight?" he asked, dropping the last baseball into her bucket.

58
00:04:00.671 --> 00:04:13.109
Kaitlyn smiled. "I can't wait!"
